  "reason": "The largest single improvement in the search came from switching the RNA encoder from pca_n2000 to scvi_n200 (0.629 → 0.715 acc, config_024 → config_036), establishing that the RNA encoder is the most impactful design choice. However, we have no evidence on whether this gain is specific to scvi's VAE-based architecture or generalizable to other learned encoders. config_048 (scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, concat) holds all other hyperparameters at their best-known values and swaps only the RNA encoder to scgpt, a generative-model-based encoder with different inductive biases. If scgpt approaches scvi's performance, it tells us 'any learned encoder ≫ PCA' and broadens the viable design space; if it lags substantially, it identifies scvi's specific representational properties as critical. Under a limited budget, resolving this encoder-architecture question is more informative than fine-tuning aggregation or fusion, which have shown only small effects so far."
